Date: Wed, 9 Sep 2026 23:50:22 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 05/18] Add attention badges on buttons

A button can now carry a Badge key naming an entry in a world-readable TOML
file, and draws a coloured marker on its bottom edge while that entry is set:

  BadgeFile = "/var/lib/claude-limits/badges.toml"
  { Text = "alpha", Action = [...], Badge = "alpha" }

The file is re-read on the existing 1s tick, and only buttons whose state
actually changed are marked dirty, so partial redraw still applies. "ask" and
"done" get distinct colours; anything else falls back to a neutral marker.

As with the widget file source, the daemon runs as `nobody` and cannot read a
user's home, so state arrives through a file written by something outside it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
